flowchart TB
  subgraph APP[Application communication — verified REST over HTTP]
    C[Client] -->|HTTP API requests :8081| A[Appointment Service]
    A -->|HTTP REST :8082| P[Patient Service]
    A -->|HTTP REST :8083| V[Availability Service]
    A -->|HTTP POST /api/notifications :8084| N[Notification Service<br/>simulates acceptance; no email or SMS delivery]
  end

  subgraph COMPOSE[Alternative 1 — Local Docker Compose deployment]
    direction TB
    CB[Four Docker images<br/>built from service Dockerfiles] --> CC[Four service containers<br/>Appointment :8081 · Patient :8082<br/>Availability :8083 · Notification :8084]
    CC --> CV[Named volumes mounted at /data<br/>appointment-data · patient-data<br/>availability-data · notification-data]
    CV --> CD[(Four independent SQLite files<br/>one database owned by each service)]
  end

  subgraph KUBE[Alternative 2 — Kubernetes on Minikube]
    direction TB
    KB[Four prebuilt images<br/>loaded into Minikube] --> KD[Four Deployments<br/>one replica each in manifests]
    KD --> KS[Kubernetes Services<br/>Appointment NodePort<br/>other services ClusterIP]
    KD --> KP[Four PVCs, each requesting 1 GiB<br/>mounted at /data in its service Pod]
    KP --> KDB[(Four independent SQLite files<br/>one database owned by each service)]
  end

  APP -. same service design, deployed separately .-> COMPOSE
  APP -. same service design, deployed separately .-> KUBE

